**Read:** [Design and Manufacturing II — MIT 2.008, 2025](../sources/Design-and-Manufacturing-II-MIT-2025.lingua#r_2FHEWYSEAHBY7X6030TW00F32E), joining lectures 9–10, then the shared metallurgy joining Record linked next. Carry forward the earlier structural-joint load analysis.

The required joint performance must survive its manufacturing process. Joint preparation, consumable, heat or force input, alignment and environment affect the delivered connection. Inspecting a final seam or bond surface cannot reveal every important condition that existed during joining.

Connect the drawing, procedure and evidence. A procedure demonstrated on a coupon has a defined material, geometry and process domain; transferring it to another thickness or restraint needs an argument. Distortion and residual stress can affect subsequent assembly even if the nominal joint strength is adequate.

**Work:** Write a physical account of one joint before, during and after production. Identify what can be measured during processing and what needs later inspection or destructive evidence. Continue into the shared material/processing study before choosing a qualification or inspection method.

**Return:** [Mechanical engineering and machine design](../Mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design.lingua#r_0017YZ63HZBZ4P4WD8DECVWE4R).
